// SEED GRAMMAR — deliberately minimal so `npm run grammar` succeeds from
// day one. Replacing it with the full Chalk v1 token grammar is P1-T2.
//
// Requirements for the real grammar (see docs/phase1-spec.md, task P1-T2):
//  - Token-level fidelity: Number, Color (#rrggbb), Angle (45° / 45deg),
//    String, keywords, Ident, Label (ident directly followed by ':'),
//    LineComment (`//` to end of line — see the example programs).
//  - Line-oriented structure only: Lezer does NOT model indentation blocks
//    (decision D12). Semantic nesting comes from the hand-rolled parser.
//  - Error tolerance: any input must produce a tree, never a thrown error.
//  - Node names referenced by styleTags in chalkLanguage.ts must exist here.

@top Program { (Number | Identifier | newline)* }

@tokens {
  Number { $[0-9]+ ("." $[0-9]+)? }
  Identifier { $[a-zA-Z_] $[a-zA-Z0-9_]* }
  newline { "\n" }
  space { $[ \t]+ }
}

@skip { space }
